---

Start with [Getting started]($link.page('docs/getting-started')), then build a
complete app in the [tutorial]($link.page('docs/tutorial')). [Concepts]($link.page('docs/concepts'))
explains how an Oriel app is put together. Already have a website?
[Wrap it]($link.page('docs/wrap')) with `oriel wrap`.

Every feature has one page, and every feature page has the same parts:
where it works, a quick start, how it works (with a diagram), examples, and
the full reference.

# [Core]($heading.id('core'))

[Commands and events]($link.page('docs/commands')) between the page and Zig,
[windows]($link.page('docs/windows')), [security]($link.page('docs/security')),
[development]($link.page('docs/development')) with hot reload, and the
[`oriel` CLI]($link.page('docs/cli')).

# [App and system]($heading.id('app-and-system'))

The [modules index]($link.page('docs/modules')) lists every module, its build
flag and where it works: [lifecycle]($link.page('docs/lifecycle')),
[deep links]($link.page('docs/deep-links')),
[permissions]($link.page('docs/permissions')), [tray]($link.page('docs/tray')),
[menus]($link.page('docs/menu')), [dialogs]($link.page('docs/dialogs')),
[notifications]($link.page('docs/notifications')), [files]($link.page('docs/files')),
[settings]($link.page('docs/store')), [SQLite]($link.page('docs/sql')),
[camera]($link.page('docs/camera')), [sharing]($link.page('docs/share')) and more.

# [Local AI]($heading.id('local-ai'))

[Local AI]($link.page('docs/local-ai')) (llama.cpp, whisper.cpp, GPU
backends), [chat]($link.page('docs/chat')), [dictation]($link.page('docs/dictation')),
[text to speech]($link.page('docs/tts')) and the OS's own
[system AI]($link.page('docs/system-ai')).

# [Native code and platforms]($heading.id('native-code-and-platforms'))

[Platform hooks]($link.page('docs/platform-hooks')) put your Kotlin,
Objective-C, Swift or Zig code inside the platform's own events;
[app extensions]($link.page('docs/extensions')) are your native code called
from Zig. Platform guides: [desktop]($link.page('docs/desktop')),
[Android]($link.page('docs/android')), [iOS]($link.page('docs/ios')).

# [Ship]($heading.id('ship'))

[Building]($link.page('docs/building')) (every `build.zig` option),
[packaging]($link.page('docs/packaging')), [signing]($link.page('docs/signing'))
and [updates]($link.page('docs/updater')).
